Improved dependency question and answer:

**Improved question:** “For one operator and one of each instrument, which steps are hands-on versus unattended, and at exactly which moments must the cabinet, microscope, centrifuge, incubator, and 37 °C water bath be free or ready? In particular, when must prewarmed reagents be ready, when may B’s cabinet work begin because A has left the cabinet, when may B’s neutralisation begin, when may each spin begin, when may each count begin, and can finishing work overlap the overnight settle?”

**Answer used for triggers:** prewarmed reagents must be ready before the first PBS rinse; B’s rinse starts when A’s rinse leaves the cabinet; A neutralisation waits for A trypsinisation and cabinet availability; B neutralisation waits for A to leave the cabinet again and B trypsinisation; B’s spin waits for B neutralisation and A spin finishing; B’s count waits for B resuspension and A’s count; each seeding waits for its count and cabinet availability; overnight settle runs unattended and overlaps cleaning and logging. I did not invent timed sub-steps for “add trypsin” or “transfer to tube” beyond the source durations, except for the clearly implied prewarming gate.

